    "id": "orbit",
    "type": "project",
    "content": "\n# Orbit - 3D Solar System Orrery\n\n**NASA Space Apps 2024 Project**\n\nOrbit is an interactive 3D Solar System Orrery designed for the web, bringing space exploration directly to classrooms and astronomy enthusiasts. Built during NASA Space Apps 2024, this project combines cutting-edge web technologies with educational content to create an immersive learning experience.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **3D Solar System Visualization**: Realistic representation of our solar system using Three.js\n- **Interactive Learning**: Explore planets, moons, and celestial bodies in real-time\n- **Educational Content**: Powered by Gemini AI for dynamic, contextual information\n- **Achievement System**: Gamified learning with medals and progress tracking\n- **Classroom Ready**: Designed specifically for educational environments\n- **Web-Based**: No installation required, accessible from any modern browser\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n- **Three.js**: 3D graphics and solar system rendering\n- **Next.js**: React framework for optimal performance\n- **Gemini AI**: Intelligent content generation and educational assistance\n- **WebGL**: Hardware-accelerated 3D graphics\n- **Modern Web APIs**: For immersive user experience\n\n## Educational Impact\n\nOrbit transforms traditional astronomy education by providing:\n\n- **Visual Learning**: Complex celestial mechanics made understandable through 3D visualization\n- **Interactive Exploration**: Students can navigate through space at their own pace\n- **Gamification**: Achievement system encourages continuous learning and exploration\n- **Accessibility**: Web-based platform ensures broad accessibility across devices and locations\n\n## Target Audience\n\n- **Educators**: Teaching astronomy and space science concepts\n- **Students**: From elementary to university level\n- **Space Enthusiasts**: Hobbyists interested in solar system exploration\n- **General Public**: Anyone curious about space and astronomy\n\n## NASA Space Apps Challenge\n\nThis project was developed as part of NASA Space Apps 2024, the world's largest global hackathon. The challenge focused on creating innovative solutions that help people understand and explore space using NASA's open data and resources.\n\nThe project demonstrates how modern web technologies can make space science more accessible and engaging for learners of all ages, bridging the gap between complex astronomical concepts and interactive digital experiences.\n",
    "processedContent": "<h1>Orbit - 3D Solar System Orrery</h1>\n<p><strong>NASA Space Apps 2024 Project</strong></p>\n<p>Orbit is an interactive 3D Solar System Orrery designed for the web, bringing space exploration directly to classrooms and astronomy enthusiasts. Built during NASA Space Apps 2024, this project combines cutting-edge web technologies with educational content to create an immersive learning experience.</p>\n<h2>Key Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>3D Solar System Visualization</strong>: Realistic representation of our solar system using Three.js</li>\n<li><strong>Interactive Learning</strong>: Explore planets, moons, and celestial bodies in real-time</li>\n<li><strong>Educational Content</strong>: Powered by Gemini AI for dynamic, contextual information</li>\n<li><strong>Achievement System</strong>: Gamified learning with medals and progress tracking</li>\n<li><strong>Classroom Ready</strong>: Designed specifically for educational environments</li>\n<li><strong>Web-Based</strong>: No installation required, accessible from any modern browser</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Technology Stack</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Three.js</strong>: 3D graphics and solar system rendering</li>\n<li><strong>Next.js</strong>: React framework for optimal performance</li>\n<li><strong>Gemini AI</strong>: Intelligent content generation and educational assistance</li>\n<li><strong>WebGL</strong>: Hardware-accelerated 3D graphics</li>\n<li><strong>Modern Web APIs</strong>: For immersive user experience</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Educational Impact</h2>\n<p>Orbit transforms traditional astronomy education by providing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Visual Learning</strong>: Complex celestial mechanics made understandable through 3D visualization</li>\n<li><strong>Interactive Exploration</strong>: Students can navigate through space at their own pace</li>\n<li><strong>Gamification</strong>: Achievement system encourages continuous learning and exploration</li>\n<li><strong>Accessibility</strong>: Web-based platform ensures broad accessibility across devices and locations</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Target Audience</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Educators</strong>: Teaching astronomy and space science concepts</li>\n<li><strong>Students</strong>: From elementary to university level</li>\n<li><strong>Space Enthusiasts</strong>: Hobbyists interested in solar system exploration</li>\n<li><strong>General Public</strong>: Anyone curious about space and astronomy</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>NASA Space Apps Challenge</h2>\n<p>This project was developed as part of NASA Space Apps 2024, the world&#39;s largest global hackathon. The challenge focused on creating innovative solutions that help people understand and explore space using NASA&#39;s open data and resources.</p>\n<p>The project demonstrates how modern web technologies can make space science more accessible and engaging for learners of all ages, bridging the gap between complex astronomical concepts and interactive digital experiences.</p>\n",
